WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.737
This example creates three variables Sales stores
one thousand costs stores

00:00:05.763 --> 00:00:11.412
eight hundred and profit is calculated from sales
minus costs Run

00:00:11.438 --> 00:00:17.165
the example in the browser and look at the printed
output Notice that Python evaluates

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:22.783
the assignments before it reaches the print
statements The profit variable does not contain

00:00:22.809 --> 00:00:27.928
a number that we typed directly It contains a value
derived from the other two

00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:33.575
variables Now change sales to twelve hundred and
fifty and predict the new

00:00:33.588 --> 00:00:39.170
profit before you run the code again This is a small
exercise but it demonstrates

00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:44.788
an important analytical idea When an input changes
every metric that depends on

00:00:44.815 --> 00:00:46.433
that input may change as well
